{
  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports Excel shows Unlicensed Product and blocks editing. Checking account status and devices per KB-026."
}

{
  "user_id": 9,
  "reason": "Checking recent sign-in results to see whether the user is signing in successfully with company account (KB-026 quick check and escalate condition)."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0109",
  "reason": "Checking laptop state and warnings for Office licensing/activation issue."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and your recent Microsoft 365 sign-ins are succeeding, so the account itself is fine. The 'Unlicensed Product' message usually means the Office license isn't assigned to your account, which needs a closer look, so I've passed your ticket to our second-level team. While you wait, you can try signing out of Office (open any Office app, go to the Word or Excel menu, choose Account, then Sign out), close all Office apps, reopen one, and sign in with your Brightline email. Please also note that your mailbox is about 99% full, which can cause problems, so clearing out some old email or attachments would help. Let us know if the banner is still there after that.",
  "internal_note": "Checked: lookup_user shows user 9 (Mei Chen, Operations) active, not blocked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11, mailbox 99.4% full (50.9 of 51.2 GB). check_signin_logs: last 10 sign-ins all successful with Duo push, m365 from corporate network and VPN from residential, all within usual hours, no anomalies. check_device_status: BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) online, 75 GB free (14.6%), no warnings. Finding: KB-026 escalation condition met (user signs in correctly but still sees Unlicensed product), so the likely cause is a missing Microsoft 365 license assignment, which I cannot verify or fix with my tools. Note that KB-026 fix steps are written for Windows (Settings > Accounts) and the device is macOS, so Tier 2 should use the Mac equivalents. Mailbox is near quota and may need attention separately. No action tools were used and no changes were made.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-026",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
